Output contract:
- parent_issue must stay feature/behavior based and non-technical.
- engineering_children must hold the technical implementation breakdown.
- project_key must be one of allowed_project_keys.
- Every parent_issue.issue_type and engineering_children.issue_type must exactly match one issue type listed for the selected project in "Jira issue types available for create by project key".
- For parent_issue.issue_type, choose the best available type for the selected project. Use Epic only for initiative-scale work.
- For engineering_children.issue_type, prefer Sub-task/Subtask when that exact type is available for the selected project and the work is clearly a child implementation ticket; otherwise use another listed implementation issue type such as Task.
- labels should be short normalized tokens when present.
- parent_issue.open_questions must be stakeholder-safe and non-technical.
- engineering_children.how_to_test must include concrete validation actions.
- when reseeding existing work, set issue_key if explicitly known from source context.
